Binary and command names are unchanged. valkey-server, valkey-cli, and
valkey-benchmark remain the primary programs. redis-server, redis-cli, and
redis-benchmark are compatibility symlinks created by `make install`, so
existing Redis and Valkey clients and tooling keep working.

Builds of this fork add an INFO server field, cmo_version, whose value is the
Valkey version plus the suffix -cmo (for example 255.255.255-cmo). The
valkey_version field stays the numeric Valkey version so protocol, replication,
and RDB version handling stay compatible.
